'' T90, RUN: A LITERAL WITH A UNICODE ESCAPE, passed straight to a BYREF string parameter, arrives
'' as its text. It is typed narrow but is wide (TermIsWide_), and the byref-descriptor path asked
'' only the type: it passed the escape's SPELLING as a narrow temporary descriptor, which a
'' 'byref ustring' callee read as UTF-16 -- len( !"\u00E4b" ) was 7, and an lcase/instr search
'' of two such literals found nothing. Converted now as a wide source is, into the parameter's own
'' flavour. Output identical to fbc-modern 1.20's, 2026-10-03. See src/mir/lowercall.bas.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/byref-escaped-literal.bas -o tests/codegen/byrefescapedlit.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/codegen/byrefescapedlit.exe
'' RUN: tests/codegen/byrefescapedlit.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  2 5 5 3
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  2 5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  12
